Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:43:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 199/215] fix: e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistRay default 24 m -> 48 m

Energy audit E8. Past MaxDistRay a ray is a MISS, and a miss does not look like
"nothing found" - it looks like a lit surface. At 24 m most of a hangar-sized
room is past the limit, so most of the mirror was showing the fallback rather
than the room, and the fallback is flatter and usually brighter than the real
surface. 48 m covers an interior; it is still a cost dial and still a cvar.

With the sky fix of bbf8f196 in front of it a distant miss is now the sky above
the horizon and the env probe below it, so what a too-short ray costs is
detail, not a second sun - but the right answer is still to reach the wall.

The registration default in SceneTreeCVars.inl is the only default that matters:
SceneTree.cpp:2798 only lets a level override these five when tiAdv.rtActive is
set, which no shipping level can do (the serialisation lines are commented out),
so the console value is in charge. The renderer has no separate default of its
own - INIT_SVO_CVAR mirrors whatever is registered here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
---
 Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/SVO/SceneTreeCVars.inl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/SVO/SceneTreeCVars.inl b/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/SVO/SceneTreeCVars.inl
index 43f49ba6..9af72f09 100644
--- a/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/SVO/SceneTreeCVars.inl
+++ b/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/SVO/SceneTreeCVars.inl
@@ -246,7 +246,7 @@ REGISTER_CVAR_AUTO(int, e_svoTI_Reflect_Vox_Max, 100, VF_NULL, "Controls amount
 REGISTER_CVAR_AUTO(int, e_svoTI_Reflect_Vox_MaxEdit, 10000, VF_NULL, "Controls amount of voxels allowed to refresh every frame during lights editing");
 REGISTER_CVAR_AUTO(int, e_svoTI_Reflect_Vox_Max_Overhead, 50, VF_NULL, "Controls amount of voxels allowed to refresh every frame");
 REGISTER_CVAR_AUTO(int, e_svoTI_RT_Active, 0, VF_EXPERIMENTAL, "Activates mesh ray tracing for reflections\nIt is necessary to re-voxelize the scene after activation");
-REGISTER_CVAR_AUTO(float, e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistRay, 24.f, VF_EXPERIMENTAL, "Maximum ray distance for mesh tracing");
+REGISTER_CVAR_AUTO(float, e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistRay, 48.f, VF_EXPERIMENTAL, "Maximum ray distance for mesh tracing. Past it the ray is a MISS and is resolved by the sky (above the horizon) or the env probe (below it), not by the surface that is actually there");
 REGISTER_CVAR_AUTO(float, e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistCam, 100.f, VF_EXPERIMENTAL, "Maximum camera distance for mesh tracing");
 REGISTER_CVAR_AUTO(float, e_svoTI_RT_MinGloss, 0.85f, VF_EXPERIMENTAL, "Minimum surface glossiness for mesh tracing");
 REGISTER_CVAR_AUTO(float, e_svoTI_RT_MinRefl, 0, VF_EXPERIMENTAL, "Minimum surface reflectance for mesh tracing");
